{"id":"8614850b-fc64-4449-8d25-037c52c9b134","object":"chat.completion","created":1789996747,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"schema\": \"amr-supervisor/v1\",\n  \"select\": [\n    {\n      \"when\": \"OwnerFree and RequestA\",\n      \"action\": \"SelectA\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"OwnerFree and RequestB\",\n      \"action\": \"SelectB\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"True\",\n      \"action\": \"Defer\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"step\": [\n    {\n      \"when\": \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\",\n      \"action\": \"Brake\",\n      \"next\": \"Stopped\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted\",\n      \"action\": \"Brake\",\n      \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"AtGoal and Released and Halted\",\n      \"action\": \"Finish\",\n      \"next\": \"Done\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"AtGoal and Released and not Halted\",\n      \"action\": \"Brake\",\n      \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ\",\n      \"action\": \"Release\",\n      \"next\": \"Traversing\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted\",\n      \"action\": \"Brake\",\n      \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"not OwnReservation and not Released\",\n      \"action\": \"Request\",\n      \"next\": \"Waiting\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"ModeStopped\",\n      \"action\": \"Resume\",\n      \"next\": \"ResumePending\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"True\",\n      \"action\": \"Proceed\",\n      \"next\": \"Traversing\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","reasoning_content":"We need answer only JSON. Need synthesize rules. Need parse policy. Need produce select rules and step rules. Need exactly root keys schema select step. select array rules with when/action. step rules with when/action/next. Max 12 each. Need cover all inputs. Need no tools. Need final JSON only.\n\nWe need design expressions limited allowed names. Need Boolean expressions. Need rules ordered by priority. Need ensure every possible input has result. For select 32 combos. Inputs: OwnerFree, RequestA, RequestB, PreferA, PreferB. Actions SelectA, SelectB, Defer.\nRequirements:\n- Selecting A requires OwnerFree and RequestA.\n- Selecting B requires OwnerFree and RequestB.\n- If reservation free and at least one request exists, select an eligible robot, rather than Defer. Otherwise Defer required.\n- When both eligible, either legal; preferences advisory not obligation.\n\nThus select rules:\n1 when OwnerFree and RequestA -> SelectA? Need if both eligible, either legal. If we always select A when A eligible, then when both A and B eligible selects A, legal. Need if OwnerFree and not RequestA and RequestB -> SelectB. If OwnerFree and RequestA -> SelectA covers both. Else Defer. But what if OwnerFree true RequestA true RequestB false -> A yes. OwnerFree true RequestA false RequestB true -> B. OwnerFree true both -> A. OwnerFree false or no requests -> Defer. So two rules + default Defer. We could include Prefer but not needed. Need every input result. Rule order maybe:\nwhen \"OwnerFree and RequestA\" -> SelectA\nwhen \"OwnerFree and RequestB\" -> SelectB\nwhen \"True\" -> Defer\nThis satisfies? If OwnerFree true RequestA true RequestB true, first SelectA. Both eligible, either legal. PreferB ignored legal. \"If reservation free and at least one request exists, select an eligible robot, rather than Defer\" yes. If A eligible but B not, A. If B eligible but not A, B. If OwnerFree and RequestA false RequestB false Defer. If OwnerFree false even Request true Defer. Good. Only 3 rules.\n\nStep more complex. Need define rules ordered by authority. Need all inputs. Step inputs: ObservationUsable, PedestrianBlocked, OwnReservation, Released, BodyClearOfZ, Halted, AtGoal, TaskActive plus mode flags. Modes one-hot: ModeIdle, ModeWaiting, ModeTraversing, ModeBrakeRequested, ModeStopped, ModeResumePending, ModeDone. Exactly one true. Step actions Request, Proceed, Brake, Resume, Release, Finish. Each rule action and next mode.\n\nPolicy:\nP2 exceptions to normal operation.\n\nordinary step outcome is Proceed, entering Traversing. It is displaced by following requirements. Authority highest to lowest:\n1 invalid/blocked/task-inactive handling;\n2 released-goal handling;\n3 whole-body release;\n4 unfinished braking;\n5 reservation request;\n6 restart transition;\n7 ordinary motion.\n\nRestart transition applies to current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending.\nA missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides restart transition.\nBrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides a missing-reservation request.\nHowever, OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\n\nHigher than all these is arrival with AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted, return Brake and enter BrakeRequested; with Halted, return Finish and enter Done.\nHighest of all, whenever ObservationUsable is false, TaskActive is false, or PedestrianBlocked is true, return Brake. Under that highest-priority condition, enter Stopped if Halted is true and BrakeRequested otherwise. Thus even an arrived and halted robot must obey this highest-priority rule if its input is blocked or invalid.\n\nThese rules apply to every input combination and mode; if multiple descriptions apply, use higher-authority requirement, without assuming that combination cannot occur physically. Select follows eligibility and totality rules.\n\nNeed determine exact step rule synthesis. Need map priorities. Let's restate layers:\n\nHighest H0: invalid/blocked/task-inactive:\nCondition C0 = (not ObservationUsable) or (not TaskActive) or PedestrianBlocked.\nAction Brake. Next = if Halted then Stopped else BrakeRequested. Because \"enter Stopped if Halted true and BrakeRequested otherwise.\" This unconditionally applies regardless of mode? \"These rules apply to every input combination and mode\" yes. So in any mode, if C0 true -> Brake to Stopped if Halted else BrakeRequested. Need perhaps two rules to set next depending Halted, or one rule cannot have conditional next. Step rule returns action and explicit next mode, next is string constant. Need split C0 and Halted, C0 and not Halted. Priority within same condition? Both same. Rule1: C0 and Halted -> Brake next Stopped. Rule2: C0 and not Halted -> Brake next BrakeRequested. Need ensure if C0 true, one matches. Halted Boolean. Good.\n\nNext priority H1: released-goal handling: \"Higher than all these is arrival with AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted, return Brake and enter BrakeRequested; with Halted, return Finish and enter Done.\" Need apply after C0? Wording: \"Higher than all these is arrival... Highest of all, whenever ...\" So C0 highest, then H1. Condition AtGoal and Released. If not C0. If Halted -> Finish next Done. If not Halted -> Brake next BrakeRequested. Does mode matter? Applies every mode. Yes. Need two rules:\nwhen not C0 and AtGoal and Released and Halted -> Finish next Done.\nwhen not C0 and AtGoal and Released and not Halted -> Brake next BrakeRequested.\nBut do we need include not C0? Since C0 rules before, if C0 true, will match first. For subsequent, no need include not C0 because first rule already handles all C0. In rule order, if C0 and AtGoal etc and Halted, first C0 Halted matches. So H1 rules can simply AtGoal and Released and Halted; AtGoal and Released and not Halted. But beware if C0 true and Halted, first matches Stopped not Finish. Good. If C0 false, H1. So no not C0 needed.\n\nNext H2: whole-body release: \"OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\" Condition OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ. Action Release next Traversing. Does priority after H1, before H3. Applies every mode except if H0/H1. So rule: when OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ -> Release next Traversing. But wait \"before unfinished braking is considered\" yes. Need if AtGoal Released? H1 higher. If C0 highest. Good.\n\nNext H3: unfinished braking: \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides a missing-reservation request.\" Condition ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted. Action Brake next BrakeRequested. (Even if OwnReservation? H2 before, so if OwnReservation & BodyClearOfZ release. The policy says H2 before unfinished braking. Yes.)\n\nNext H4: reservation request: \"A missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides the restart transition.\" Condition not OwnReservation and not Released. Action Request next Waiting. But note H2 condition OwnReservation and BodyClear. H4 only if no own and no released. It overrides restart transition H5. Applies after unfinished braking. Need include? If ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted and missing reservation, H3 wins Brake. If not H3, request. Good.\n\nNext H5: restart transition: current Stopped mode yields Resume, entering ResumePending. Condition ModeStopped. Action Resume next ResumePending. But H4 missing reservation overrides restart. So after H4, if ModeStopped and not (missing reservation)? Actually if ModeStopped and missing reservation, H4 Request. If ModeStopped and OwnReservation or Released true, restart Resume. But H2 might apply if OwnReservation & BodyClearOfZ -> Release. H3 only if ModeBrakeRequested. H1 maybe. So H5 rule can be ModeStopped -> Resume next ResumePending, placed after H4. But need if ModeStopped and OwnReservation & BodyClearOfZ, H2 Release before H5. If ModeStopped and AtGoal Released H1. If C0 H0. Good.\n\nNext H6: ordinary motion: default Proceed entering Traversing. For all remaining inputs. Action Proceed next Traversing.\n\nNeed also consider \"released-goal handling\" AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted Brake, with Halted Finish. If Halted and AtGoal Released, Finish. If not Halted Brake. What about H2 OwnReservation BodyClear if AtGoal Released? H1 higher. Good.\n\nNeed ensure every possible step input has result. We can include default Proceed at end. Need order. There are up to maybe 10 rules:\n1 C0 and Halted -> Brake Stopped\n2 C0 and not Halted -> Brake BrakeRequested\n3 AtGoal and Released and Halted -> Finish Done\n4 AtGoal and Released and not Halted -> Brake BrakeRequested\n5 OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ -> Release Traversing\n6 ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted -> Brake BrakeRequested\n7 not OwnReservation and not Released -> Request Waiting\n8 ModeStopped -> Resume ResumePending\n9 True -> Proceed Traversing\n\nNeed check priority order exactly: Policy authority from highest to lowest: invalid/blocked/task-inactive; released-goal; whole-body release; unfinished braking; reservation request; restart transition; ordinary motion. Yes.\n\nNeed be careful about \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides a missing-reservation request.\" If mode BrakeRequested and not Halted, rule 6 before reservation request. Good.\n\nBut \"However, OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\" Rule 5 before rule 6. Good.\n\nNeed include C0 expression exactly. Allowed names: ObservationUsable, PedestrianBlocked, OwnReservation, Released, BodyClearOfZ, Halted, AtGoal, TaskActive, mode flags. No comparisons. Use not, and, or. Python precedence: not > and > or. Parentheses allowed. Need within 512 chars and AST nodes/depth. We'll keep simple.\n\nC0 = \"(not ObservationUsable) or (not TaskActive) or PedestrianBlocked\". Need ensure no extra. Python Boolean precedence: not binds tight, or. Parentheses okay. Could write \"not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked\". Fine.\n\nRules:\n1 when \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\" action Brake next Stopped.\n2 when \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted\" action Brake next BrakeRequested.\nNeed note Python precedence: \"not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked and Halted\" would be wrong due and precedence. Use parentheses.\n\n3 when \"AtGoal and Released and Halted\" action Finish next Done. But if C0 true and Halted, rule1 catches. If C0 false, okay. If C0 true and Halted, not Finish. If C0 true and not Halted, rule2. Good.\n4 when \"AtGoal and Released and not Halted\" action Brake next BrakeRequested.\n\n5 when \"OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ\" action Release next Traversing.\n6 when \"ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted\" action Brake next BrakeRequested.\n7 when \"not OwnReservation and not Released\" action Request next Waiting.\n8 when \"ModeStopped\" action Resume next ResumePending.\n9 when \"True\" action Proceed next Traversing.\n\nNeed check if any higher rule unexpectedly overrides H4 in cases where should not. Example ModeStopped, missing reservation (neither own nor released): Rule7 before rule8 -> Request Waiting. Good. Example ModeStopped, OwnReservation true, Released false, BodyClear false. Rule7 condition false (OwnReservation true), Rule8 -> Resume. According to missing reservation requires Request when neither OwnReservation nor Released. Since OwnReservation true, not missing. Restart transition applies. Good.\nExample ModeStopped, OwnReservation false, Released true, BodyClear false. Rule7 false (Released true), Rule8 -> Resume. Is restart transition allowed with Released true? Policy says missing reservation when neither OwnReservation nor Released true. If Released true, no missing reservation, restart transition applies unless higher. Released maybe acknowledged release; ModeStopped? Hmm maybe if Released true and AtGoal? H1. If no AtGoal, restart. Yes.\nExample ModeStopped, OwnReservation true, BodyClear true -> Rule5 Release Traversing before restart. Good.\nExample ModeStopped, ModeBrakeRequested? impossible one-hot, but no need infer. If both? They said exactly one mode flag true. But formal evaluation all combinations? Wait \"All 32 combinations of select facts and all 7 * 256 combinations of mode and step facts are evaluated\" Actually 7 * 256 suggests for each mode flag, 256 step fact combos, mode exactly one. So no both. Fine.\n\nNeed consider \"No special terminal-mode shortcut exists: requirements apply in every mode, including Done.\" Our rules apply regardless of mode except mode conditions. Good. In Done, if C0 -> Brake etc; if AtGoal Released -> Finish; if OwnReservation BodyClear -> Release; if ModeBrakeRequested? Mode done false; missing reservation -> Request; else Proceed Traversing. So Done can transition out. Is that okay? Policy says apply every mode, ordinary outcome Proceed Traversing. Yes.\n\nNeed maybe \"released-goal handling\" has condition AtGoal and Released both true. But maybe if Halted false, return Brake and enter BrakeRequested. If Halted true, Finish Done. We did.\n\nPotential issue: Rule 5 OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ requires Release entering Traversing before unfinished braking. But what if H4 missing reservation? OwnReservation true so H4 not. Good.\nPotential issue: Rule 5 before H3. If ModeBrakeRequested not Halted and OwnReservation BodyClear, policy says H2 whole-body release before unfinished braking. So Release. Good.\nPotential issue: Rule 5 before H1? No, H1 higher. So if AtGoal Released Halted and OwnReservation BodyClear, H1 Finish. Our order has H1 before H2. Good.\nPotential issue: C0 highest. If C0 true and Halted, action Brake next Stopped. If AtGoal Released also true, H0 wins. Good.\nPotential issue: C0 and Halted false -> BrakeRequested. If AtGoal Released Halted false also, H0 wins same action/next. No conflict.\n\nNeed maybe combine C0 rules? Could use default? But okay. Max 9.\n\nNeed ensure JSON valid. No comments. Exactly one JSON object. Need include schema \"amr-supervisor/v1\". select array. step array.\n\nNeed decide whether select should use preferences? Policy says preferences advisory; no obligation. We can ignore. But maybe select must use all names? No. The select function may refer to PreferA/PreferB, but not required. Need ensure \"When both robots are eligible, either is legal; preferences do not impose an additional acceptance obligation, and their values may conflict or both be absent.\" Our deterministic choose A when both eligible is legal. Does \"PreferA/PreferB are advisory\" mean if PreferB true and both eligible, should select B? Wording: \"When both robots are eligible, either is legal; preferences do not impose an additional acceptance obligation, and their values may conflict or both be absent.\" It says preferences do not impose acceptance obligation. So ignoring is fine. \"If reservation free and at least one request exists, select an eligible robot, rather than Defer.\" We do.\n\nNeed ensure select total: Rules:\nwhen \"OwnerFree and RequestA\" action \"SelectA\"\nwhen \"OwnerFree and RequestB\" action \"SelectB\"\nwhen \"True\" action \"Defer\"\nIf OwnerFree true RequestA false RequestB false -> Defer. If OwnerFree false RequestA true -> first false? OwnerFree and RequestA false. second false. default Defer. Good. If OwnerFree true RequestA true RequestB true -> SelectA. Both eligible. Good.\n\nNeed maybe include PreferA if OwnerFree and RequestA and PreferA? But no.\n\nNow step expressions. Need verify syntax constraints. Rule 1:\n\"when\": \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\"\nAction Brake next Stopped.\nRule 2:\n\"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted\"\nAction Brake next BrakeRequested.\nRule 3:\n\"AtGoal and Released and Halted\"\nAction Finish next Done.\nRule 4:\n\"AtGoal and Released and not Halted\"\nAction Brake next BrakeRequested.\nRule 5:\n\"OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ\"\nAction Release next Traversing.\nRule 6:\n\"ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted\"\nAction Brake next BrakeRequested.\nRule 7:\n\"not OwnReservation and not Released\"\nAction Request next Waiting.\nRule 8:\n\"ModeStopped\"\nAction Resume next ResumePending.\nRule 9:\n\"True\"\nAction Proceed next Traversing.\n\nNeed consider if rule 7 should include \"and not (OwnReservation or Released)\"? Equivalent \"not OwnReservation and not Released\". Allowed. Good.\n\nPotential subtlety: \"A missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides the restart transition.\" This is priority 5, after unfinished braking. But \"missing reservation\" condition maybe also requires TaskActive? No, if TaskActive false C0 already Brake. If Observation invalid C0. If PedestrianBlocked C0. So okay. If TaskActive true and valid and not blocked, then request. Good.\n\nPotential subtlety: \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides a missing-reservation request.\" Condition \"BrakeRequested\" could mean current mode BrakeRequested? It says \"BrakeRequested without Halted\" likely mode. Use ModeBrakeRequested. Good.\n\nPotential subtlety: \"restart transition applies to a current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending.\" Condition ModeStopped. Good.\n\nPotential subtlety: \"ordinary step outcome is Proceed, entering Traversing.\" Default True. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"Exactly one such mode flag is true.\" Our rule 8 ModeStopped. If ModeStopped false and no other higher, default Proceed. For modes Idle, Waiting, Traversing, ResumePending, Done, ordinary Proceed entering Traversing. Is that intended? Let's infer from policy. It only mentions exceptions. Ordinary outcome is Proceed, entering Traversing. So yes even from Done? They explicitly say no terminal-mode shortcut. So Done can Proceed to Traversing if no exceptions. Is that weird? They require.\n\nLet's test some scenarios:\n- Mode Idle, all step facts false? ObservationUsable true? If all false, TaskActive false triggers C0 -> Brake next BrakeRequested (if Halted false). That means if TaskActive false, always Brake. Is that intended? \"invalid/blocked/task-inactive handling\" yes TaskActive false -> Brake. So if TaskActive false, no ordinary. If TaskActive true and ObservationUsable true, PedestrianBlocked false, OwnReservation false, Released false, BodyClear false, Halted false, AtGoal false, ModeIdle: rules 1-6 false, 7 true -> Request Waiting. This matches missing reservation. If OwnReservation true, BodyClear false, ModeIdle: 1-6 false, 7 false, 8 false, default Proceed Traversing. Is that ordinary? If has reservation and not body clear, no release, no brake, no request, no restart, proceed. Yes ordinary motion.\n- Mode BrakeRequested, not Halted, OwnReservation false Released false: rule6 -> Brake BrakeRequested, overriding request. Good.\n- Mode BrakeRequested, Halted true, OwnReservation false Released false: rule1? C0 false. rule3? AtGoal Released false. rule5? OwnRes false. rule6 false (Halted). rule7 true -> Request Waiting. Is that correct? \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake ...\" If Halted true, unfinished braking done. Then missing reservation requires Request. Yes. If OwnReservation true, Halted true, BodyClear false, ModeBrakeRequested: rule7 false, rule8 false, default Proceed Traversing. Hmm from BrakeRequested with halted and own reservation, ordinary Proceed? Maybe after halt, if not stopped mode, maybe should Proceed? Policy only says BrakeRequested without Halted continues Brake. With Halted and own reservation, no exception, ordinary Proceed. Is that intended? Maybe yes.\n- Mode Stopped, Halted true, OwnReservation false Released false: rule7 request Waiting. Missing reservation overrides restart. Good.\n- Mode Stopped, Halted true, OwnReservation true, BodyClear false: rule8 Resume ResumePending. Good.\n- Mode Stopped, Halted false, OwnReservation true, BodyClear false: rule8 Resume ResumePending. Restart transition? Does it require Halted? Policy says restart transition applies to current Stopped mode and yields Resume. No Halted condition. Even if not Halted? But current Stopped mode likely implies halted, but they say do not infer. Policy says applies to current Stopped mode. So yes.\n- Mode Stopped, Halted false, OwnReservation false Released false: rule7 Request Waiting overrides restart. Good.\n- Mode Stopped, AtGoal Released true Halted false: rule4 Brake BrakeRequested. Higher than restart. Good.\n- Mode Stopped, AtGoal Released true Halted true: rule3 Finish Done. Good.\n- C0 true, Halted true, AtGoal Released true: rule1 Brake Stopped. Highest. Good.\n\nNeed consider if rule 1 and 2 order: If C0 and Halted false, rule1 false, rule2 true. If C0 and Halted true, rule1 true. Good.\nNeed check AST nodes and depth. Fine.\n\nNow final JSON. Need no markdown. Ensure UTF-8. We can output compact or pretty. It says exactly one UTF-8 JSON object, no Markdown fences, explanatory prose. Pretty is okay as JSON. Need ensure no additional fields. Root exactly schema, select, step. Each rule exactly when/action for select; step exactly when/action/next. We must not include extra fields. Duplicate keys no.\n\nLet's craft JSON:\n\n{\n  \"schema\": \"amr-supervisor/v1\",\n  \"select\": [\n    {\"when\": \"OwnerFree and RequestA\", \"action\": \"SelectA\"},\n    {\"when\": \"OwnerFree and RequestB\", \"action\": \"SelectB\"},\n    {\"when\": \"True\", \"action\": \"Defer\"}\n  ],\n  \"step\": [\n    {\"when\": \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\", \"action\": \"Brake\", \"next\": \"Stopped\"},\n    {\"when\": \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted\", \"action\": \"Brake\", \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"},\n    {\"when\": \"AtGoal and Released and Halted\", \"action\": \"Finish\", \"next\": \"Done\"},\n    {\"when\": \"AtGoal and Released and not Halted\", \"action\": \"Brake\", \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"},\n    {\"when\": \"OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ\", \"action\": \"Release\", \"next\": \"Traversing\"},\n    {\"when\": \"ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted\", \"action\": \"Brake\", \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"},\n    {\"when\": \"not OwnReservation and not Released\", \"action\": \"Request\", \"next\": \"Waiting\"},\n    {\"when\": \"ModeStopped\", \"action\": \"Resume\", \"next\": \"ResumePending\"},\n    {\"when\": \"True\", \"action\": \"Proceed\", \"next\": \"Traversing\"}\n  ]\n}\n\nNeed verify if \"not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked\" within parentheses. The expression \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\" due precedence: (not ObservationUsable) or (not TaskActive) or PedestrianBlocked? Actually inside parentheses, \"not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked\" is (not ObservationUsable) or (not TaskActive) or PedestrianBlocked. Good. The whole is (...) and Halted. Good.\nRule 2 similar with and not Halted. Due precedence, \"not Halted\" is unary. Good.\n\nPotential issue: In Python, \"not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked\" with no parentheses? We have parentheses. Good.\n\nNeed consider if \"ModeStopped\" rule should be after missing reservation. We have. But what about \"restart transition applies to current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending. A missing reservation requires Request ... overrides restart transition.\" Good.\n\nNeed consider if \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake ... overrides missing-reservation request.\" Our rule6 before rule7. Good. But what if ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted and OwnReservation BodyClear? Rule5 before rule6. Policy: OwnReservation + BodyClear requires Release before unfinished braking. Good. What if ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted and AtGoal Released Halted? H1 before. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"Higher than all these is arrival with AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted, return Brake and enter BrakeRequested; with Halted, return Finish and enter Done.\" Our H1 rules do not include not C0. If C0 true, C0 rules catch. If C0 false, H1. Good. But what if C0 true and AtGoal Released Halted false: Rule2 Brake BrakeRequested. Same as H1. If C0 true and Halted true: Rule1 Brake Stopped, not Finish. Highest says C0. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"Highest of all, whenever ObservationUsable is false, TaskActive is false, or PedestrianBlocked is true, return Brake. Under that highest-priority condition, enter Stopped if Halted is true and BrakeRequested otherwise.\" Our C0 rules include Halted and not Halted. If Halted is true -> Stopped. If Halted false -> BrakeRequested. Good.\n\nNeed ensure select no step names. We use OwnerFree RequestA RequestB. Good. Step no select names. We use none. Good.\n\nNow maybe there is a requirement \"At most 32 total branches are allowed; per-function limit 12.\" Branches maybe number of rules? We have 12 total? select 3 + step 9 = 12. Good. \"At most 32 total branches\" okay.\n\nNeed maybe \"Source size at most 200 * 1024\" okay.\n\nNeed maybe \"Both functions are arrays of ordered rules, with at most twelve rules in each function.\" We have select 3, step 9.\n\nNeed final only JSON. Ensure no markdown. Done.\n\nBut before final, let's deeply analyze if there are any hidden pitfalls. We need synthesize restricted supervisory program. The policy presentation P2. We need ensure exact priority. Let's parse phrase by phrase.\n\n\"Policy presentation P2: exceptions to normal operation.\n\nThe ordinary step outcome is Proceed, entering Traversing. It is displaced by the following requirements. Their authority, from highest to lowest, is: invalid/blocked/task-inactive handling; released-goal handling; whole-body release; unfinished braking; reservation request; restart transition; ordinary motion.\n\nThe restart transition applies to a current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending. A missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides the restart transition. BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides a missing-reservation request. However, OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\n\nHigher than all these is arrival with AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted, return Brake and enter BrakeRequested; with Halted, return Finish and enter Done. Highest of all, whenever ObservationUsable is false, TaskActive is false, or PedestrianBlocked is true, return Brake. Under that highest-priority condition, enter Stopped if Halted is true and BrakeRequested otherwise. Thus even an arrived and halted robot must obey this highest-priority rule if its input is blocked or invalid.\n\nThese rules apply to every input combination and mode; if multiple descriptions apply, use the higher-authority requirement, without assuming that the combination cannot occur physically. Select follows the eligibility and totality rules in the interface.\"\n\nThe phrase \"Higher than all these is arrival...\" Wait they say \"Higher than all these\" after describing whole-body, unfinished, reservation, restart. But earlier they list authority: invalid/blocked/task-inactive; released-goal; whole-body release; unfinished braking; reservation request; restart transition; ordinary motion. So released-goal (arrival) is second. Then they say \"Higher than all these is arrival...\" meaning higher than the lower ones, but not higher than highest. Then \"Highest of all...\" So yes.\n\nPotential subtlety: